<!--
    GRTubeYou: the soft darkening under the controls.

    The progress bar, the button row and the time block all sit on the video with nothing behind
    them, which is why they read as controls floating over a picture rather than as one band.
    This gradient runs from fully transparent, three quarters of the way up, to 0xD0 at the very
    bottom - enough to hold white text and the thin progress line over a bright frame, and not
    so much that the lower third of the video goes grey.

    It deliberately has no top edge. The fade begins well above the progress bar, so the
    transition from picture to darkened area is gradual, which is the whole point - a scrim with
    a visible starting line is worse than no scrim.
-->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:shape="rectangle">
    <gradient
        android:angle="90"
        android:startColor="#D0000000"
        android:centerColor="#8A000000"
        android:endColor="#00000000"
        android:type="linear" />
</shape>